{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery","id":1479151,"title":"Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-19T17:23:17-07:00","id":1479151,"title":"Sorcery","content":"I only possess WTA and VTM books, it talk about people able to use &quot;magic&quot; but there not enough informations about them in those.<br /> I've found few things on different forum, there's the Sorcery that anyone can learn including werewolves (one uktena tribe if i'm correct) and maybe vampires (didn't find any clear indication for them), and there's Magic that only Mage can use and is more powerfull than Sorcery.<br /> <br /> I'm looking to create a NPC Sorcerer but as i don't know how they use Sorcery or what kind of roll they make to use it and if they have a reserve of mana i cannot finish.<br /> <br /> Is there any recent book that give those informations (all my books are v20)<br /> <br /> And what are the limit of sorcery exactly comparing to Magic? Some wiki states that the Alchemy path can at level 5 allow the sorcerer to create potion or at least chemicals able to turn the user into vampire, werewolves or Mage ( <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_(MTAs\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_(MTAs</a>) ) as i don't know much about magic i can't figure how it would be more potent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T17:55:40-07:00","id":1479152,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/347222/Sorcerer-Paths-of-Power?filters=45622_45629\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer: Paths of Power</a> from The Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what information, if any, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/194952/W20-Kinfolk-A-Breed-Apart\" target=\"_blank\">Kinfolk: A Breed Apart</a> has on the subject. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T18:26:52-07:00","id":1479154,"title":"","content":"The original way sorcery was handled in the WoD was basically a mortal's version of Thaumaturgy. Sorcerer Revised, and the STV project linked above, expanded on that idea, but keep the core idea of having Paths rated 1-5 that allow for more potent hedge magician arts, and more access to rituals. The big addition in Revised in terms of capability was the idea of very rare sorcerers that mastered a 6th dot in their paths, granting them powers that could even outdo some of the things &quot;full&quot; splats can do (though sorcery Numina Paths are not simple affairs to enact even if their specialization can be more effective than general power).<br /> <br /> KABA does have some Kinfolk specific Paths as well (as did its predecessor Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes).<br /> <br /> As NPCs, the limits on sorcery are basically what you want them to be. With enough time and study, a sorcerer could have power rivaling the dynamic magic of mages, and even surpassed them in a few ways. The big drawback is that sorcerers suck at &quot;fast&quot; effects and generally need to pre-prep things for anything really potent. As well their rituals tend to be more intensive.<br /> <br /> As PCs? Expect a power level slightly behind Thaumaturgy (esp. not being able to rely on one trait for powering Path powers, and one for rolling rituals, each Path is going to have its own roll). It's worth noting that Garou learning Paths is not impossible, but difficult enough that there's a 7-dot Merit to get access to it in some editions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T00:01:31-07:00","id":1479164,"title":"","content":"The best official published material on mortal sorcery for 20th anniversary edition is in Hunters Hunted II<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114261/V20-The-Hunters-Hunted-II\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ters-Hunted-II</a><br /> <br /> That said the book No One of Consequence recommended is based directly on the previous editions\u2019 sorcery books.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer can definitely not turn anyone into an Awakened Mage. Turning a non-werewolf into a werewolf would require the Wyrm-rite of Skindancing with the skins of slain Garou. Turning someone into a vampire with a potion is something that has been done in canon provided you have vitae as an ingredient for said potion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-20-2022, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T01:06:24-07:00","id":1479166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery?p=1479164#post1479164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sorcerer can definitely not turn anyone into an Awakened Mage. Turning a non-werewolf into a werewolf would require the Wyrm-rite of Skindancing with the skins of slain Garou. Turning someone into a vampire with a potion is something that has been done in canon provided you have vitae as an ingredient for said potion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wiki said that for the 6th rank of Alchemy so i thought that was possible to them without needing the skindancing rite, like the rank 6 is a legendary level of skill","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T05:32:17-07:00","id":1479167,"title":"","content":"I also remembered that Alchemy 6 would allow to awaken a sorcerer, but that would be wrong. There is however a sentence in the general description, reading: The highest level of Alchemy theoretically expands beyond material things; in game terms, an Alchemist who reaches this exalted state may Awaken and continue his road with the Spheres.<br /> <br /> But the older WoD Sorcerer also clearly states that sorcery is completely replaced by spheres (or disciplines, or arcanoi) if the sorcerer awakens (or is embraced or dies).<br /> <br /> The older WoD Sorcerer, as opposed to Sorcerer revised, is a bit less refined when it comes to power levels and metaphysics...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T06:49:41-07:00","id":1479168,"title":"","content":"The 6th rank of Alchemy is it's own can of worms.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer: Revised does say that you're, supposedly, cappable of transforming into any splat. It does mention werewolves, vampires and mages. However, the specifics of the ritual (bc it's a ritual) are left to the ST. The wording it's vague, and the book doesn't say what ingredients are needed, and offers no actual systems nor rules for the transformation. In no place says that the ritual should be unconditional, nor devoid of consequences. <br /> <br /> So, it could very well be that the Sorcerer would need to do something <i>similar </i>to the Wyrm-rite, with <i>similar </i>consequences. At the very least, such level should allow someone to research that transformation independantly. The Sorcerer could discover a different way of achieving the transformation, even. But, ultimately, it's ST discretion.<br /> <br /> This capability is an artifact of Revised, BUT no 20th anniversary book has truly retconned it. It's just not present, but neither was it present in most books of Revised. 20th anniversary edition doesn't have a new system for Sorcery, so that we could unequivocally say that such powers were deliberately ignored. 20th just rescues the most common &quot;system&quot; for paths, that it's similar to that of vampires, and that was present in most editions and books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T09:04:31-07:00","id":1479173,"title":"","content":"It depends.<br /> <br /> If you're just trying to make a quick and dirty sorcerer NPC, the hunters hunted and paths of power are good enough.<br /> <br /> Both the above use a nerfed version of &quot;npc&quot; sorcery. Non-sorcerer books like Halls of Arcanum, Hunters Hunted, and A Breed Apart have a much weaker version of sorcery than actual the sorcerer books(which has been true since 2nd edition). Paths of power doesn't update the mechanics either, it's just a complication of paths found in non-sorcerer books for WoD20(which aren't updates on Sorcerer revised, they're NPC powers for a out-of-splat characters) with some of the powers taken from Sorcerer revised, Sorcerer's companion in the STvault, and some new paths the writer thought up.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't recommend any of the above if you ever have a player wants to be a sorcerer. In that case, I say just pick up Sorcerer revised and tweak things to reflect the power level of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T09:12:43-07:00","id":1479174,"title":"","content":"Sorcery Revised or the STV book Paths to Power would be the best bet since they're most recent but while similar they take very different views on the concept and how the paths are implemented (Alchemy being a prime example of one of the complicated aspects of Revised.) Which suits you probably depends on the kind of Sorcerer you intended to build. Both feature the 'struggling awake' merit which covers what is essentially a wild talent you have a bit more control over at times (IIRC PtP even treats it as a wild talent mechanics-wise.) PtP also has a merit that allows certain rotes as a sort of magical gift (sort of like the Proximi from Awakened I think.) What you sound like seems like its leaning towards wild talent.<br /> <br /> If you gave M20 'Gods and Monsters' there's a short section on hedge magicians that give rough rules to approximate hedge magic/sorcerery that might give you ideas on how to simulate paths. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T10:13:37-07:00","id":1479177,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s an M20 Sorcerer book coming out soon that might answer your question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T11:52:40-07:00","id":1479182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery#post1479151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking to create a NPC Sorcerer but as i don't know how they use Sorcery or what kind of roll they make to use it and if they have a reserve of mana i cannot finish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is only an NPC and you're not looking for rules for a PC, you can do the same thing that the books do when they show one of the other splats in their Antagonists chapter - give them whatever powers already in the corebook that can emulate that. This is why Lupines in Vampire are shown having Vampire disciplines, and why vampires in Werewolf are given Gifts. It's not that these creatures actually have those powers. It's just an easy way for the ST to run those creatures if they don't have access to those other books.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to do that and want the actual rules for Sorcerer, that's fine. The other posters have given you some options. But if you just want to be able to run your plot, then just give that NPC Sorcerer a combination of Thaumaturgy Paths and some appropriate Gifts (since you have both Vampire and Werewolf books) that give your NPC the powers you want him to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T13:44:03-07:00","id":1479194,"title":"","content":"I've bought &quot;sorcerer path of power&quot; and MTA to complete my game.<br /> Reading mage is absolutly awesome but as far as i know the true reality of universe is known from werewolf since they can freely travel accross spiritual realm and ask the story of the reality to their creator. What i mean is that according to their legends Cain was made immortal by the weaver and become undead and full vampire by feeding on the wyrm's flesh, so is there any legend that state the apparition of mage?<br /> <br /> From what i have read they seems to be able to use same ability than the trinity but by doing so their tricks clash with the laws of the trinity, and they call that paradox. So being a mage mean that we have access to the trinity's powers but if that's right how can they loose it by turning into vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-20T15:46:55-07:00","id":1479197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery?p=1479194#post1479194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've bought &amp;quot;sorcerer path of power&amp;quot; and MTA to complete my game.<br /> Reading mage is absolutly awesome but as far as i know the true reality of universe is known from werewolf since they can freely travel accross spiritual realm and ask the story of the reality to their creator. What i mean is that according to their legends Cain was made immortal by the weaver and become undead and full vampire by feeding on the wyrm's flesh, so is there any legend that state the apparition of mage?<br /> <br /> From what i have read they seems to be able to use same ability than the trinity but by doing so their tricks clash with the laws of the trinity, and they call that paradox. So being a mage mean that we have access to the trinity's powers but if that's right how can they loose it by turning into vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one possible interpretation. <br /> <br /> But consider that Garou generally don't get to speak directly with the true creators of the universe found within their mythology. They don't get to ask Gaia, the Weaver, the Wyld, or the Wyrm for proof that their legends are true. They don't generally get to speak to anything higher ranking than an Incarna, and even the answers given by them tend to be limited to rumour and hearsay for most members of the Changing Breeds. And of course, their answers could be mistaken, or lies that serve their purposes.<br /> <br /> And Mages are quite capable of wandering the Umbra in search of answers as well, though most have a hard time accessing some of the Realms known to the Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> There isn't really any hard canon that gives a definite answer about whether canon in Werewolf or Mage is more &quot;true&quot; than the other. It's pretty much left up to the Storyteller to make that decision, depending on which gameline they're running and what kind of Story they want to Tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T00:40:10-07:00","id":1479219,"title":"","content":"Another thing that i can't get is how exctly paradox work: as it's described a mage control reality and if his tricks are too powerfull or not well &quot;included&quot; in reality (the focus: using a punch and including some magick in it to get more effect) then reality hit them with paradox. But in the mean time that paradox in reality depend on the sleepers mind? It is said in the book that if you're in a city where people believes you can fly on a brood then if a mage do so he will not be paradoxed...<br /> <br /> No i can't get it, to me they have to use focus to fool reality and make it think that the mage is using his law, i see it like a poker game with the universe: if you can cheat without being caught then good for you but if your cheat is too obvious or big then universe will kick your *ss. But how in the world could it be defined by sleepers way of thinking? <br /> <br /> That kind of rule appear to me like an obvious game balancing system more than a realistic lore explanation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 04-21-2022, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T01:59:41-07:00","id":1479223,"title":"","content":"Well, because according to mage, reality is not objective but the consensus of all people's believes about what is real in a given region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T02:54:06-07:00","id":1479229,"title":"","content":"To put it another way, you are playing poker against the universe, but the universe's casinos, gambling dens, and friends getting together at one person's house for a private game all change what it takes to be a good cheat. Most of Earth operates on big name casino conditions: lots of cameras and security watching for any cheaters, meaning you have to be really subtle and really know the way things work to avoid getting caught (or just cheat and try to get away with everything you can before you get kicked out). If you search them out, you can find smaller operations where they don't have that kind of security, and rely on social norms to keep people honest; they're easier to cheat, but also ready to boot you if you don't fit in (these are major Reality Zones). And you can even setup your own home gambling room for you and your buddies where it's really easy to cheat things because it's yours (aka a Sanctum).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T05:48:01-07:00","id":1479236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery?p=1479194#post1479194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what i have read they seems to be able to use same ability than the trinity but by doing so their tricks clash with the laws of the trinity, and they call that paradox. So being a mage mean that we have access to the trinity's powers but if that's right how can they loose it by turning into vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because mages do magic(k) through a special type of creature or entity that Mage calls &quot;Avatars&quot;. These Avatars are part of the mage's soul, but break that connection uppon the mage's death and &quot;reincarnate&quot; on a different human.<br /> <br /> Also, they generally react in negative ways to the mage becoming a different supernatural creature, albeit *what* happens and *why* it's often unclear (OOC, it's because WoD has a very serious: &quot;no stacking splats&quot; rule. It has few exceptions, and usually ones that include dire penalties for the character).<br /> <br /> In the case of vampirism, it's believed that either the vampiric condition it's somehow damaging to Avatars, and they shatter after the embrace ,OR that, since becomming a vampire requires one to die first, they just leave on death like they always do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-21-2022, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T06:25:23-07:00","id":1479237,"title":"","content":"One explanation regarding Garou was, that Gaia is somewhat of a shared Avatar of the shapeshifters and that therefore they do not become awaken as mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T10:46:33-07:00","id":1479250,"title":"","content":"Or the much simpler explanation: you need to be human to Awaken, and while &quot;what is human?&quot; can be blurry, a Garou is solidly on the &quot;not human&quot; side of things metaphysically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T11:22:26-07:00","id":1479251,"title":"","content":"It is indeed impossible for a Garou to awaken since they are not human and it is why you cannot have a Vampire Mage or Changeling, Mummy, Wraith, Demon, etc. Now as to whether they can learn Sorcery depends on the edition and what the ST decides. The official answer is &quot;no, but maybe&quot;. Garou have gifts and their gnosis prevents them from accurately learning sorcery, though some Uktena, Bastet, and Kitsune can practice their own version of sorcery (called shadow magic/sorcery for Bastet) but even among these three tribes it is rare. Vampires have vitae and blood sorcery that replaces normal sorcery (though they could learn a merit in older editions that lets them use sorcery if they knew it before they were embraced). Changeling have their own version of sorcery called Arts. Wraith are dead and use Arcanoi. Mummy's have Haku that replaces sorcery. Demons use their Lore for various effects.<br /> <br /> Now some have argued Mages should be able to use sorcery, but that is also impossible. An awakening Avatar could never make use of sorcery and if a Mage tried to, the Avatar would instantly convert it over to sphere magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 04-21-2022, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T13:00:39-07:00","id":1479258,"title":"","content":"For the most part... sorcery also just kinda sucks compared to most full splat powers. The primary reason, in-game and for players, to pursue sorcery is because it's capable of filling gaps their character type normally can't deal with. For the Garou and Fera, seeking out sorcery is rare because they're socially and mechanically encouraged to stay in their lanes. That's why it's only the particularly occult-curious shifters that are noted for bothered to actually try to learn these things. Knowing rare weird shit is their lane, and sorcery offers a few tricks that aren't necessarily easily found in Gifts and Rites (esp. if you're not high enough Rank yet).<br /> <br /> The biggest reason I try to steer players away from sorcery if they're already playing a supernatural creature? So they don't waste the XP. Sorcery isn't worth the price of admission to most supernaturals compared to sticking to their normal powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T13:39:46-07:00","id":1479262,"title":"","content":"Quick question about Mage's magick, the spheres are pillars of reality, and according to Garou's lore the reality has been forged by the Triat. Does Triat using sphere to interact with universe, or are the sphere the creation of the Triat to &quot;maintain&quot; their work together?<br /> <br /> Also i couldn't help myself but to try and assign sphere to the Triat and Ga\u00efa but i can't state on which sphere belong to whom:<br /> <br /> Ga\u00efa as the Life incarnation would be Life and Mind because the're all the base of any living being<br /> Wyld would be Forces (impredictable) and Prime(pure creation)<br /> Weaver would be Correspondance and Time<br /> Wyrm would be Enthropy (obviously) and Matter (to corrupt it with enthropy)<br /> <br /> All of them share Spirit since the Triat are all 3 spirits and use them to interact with the world and the Ferae<br /> <br /> The Triat, as living godly entity can freely play with some spheres that belong to the other; the wyrm seems to be able to use matter or life to corrupt humans, The Wyld can use Matter to transform thing into other etc...<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T14:01:56-07:00","id":1479265,"title":"","content":"The Spheres aren't &quot;pillars of reality,&quot; and the Trait have no need of them. The Spheres are a way mages conceptualize the universe as seen through their Awakened understanding. The current Spheres have not always been the way mage's magic worked, and they slowly adapt over time as well (as seen by things like the rise of variant Spheres mostly in the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> Remember that, to mages, belief is a central part of how they interact with the universe. As mages started to gather, share what they knew, and forming common beliefs around how magic works, they weren't just seeing the universe for how it was, but shaping the universe into what they believed at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T22:01:53-07:00","id":1479679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery?p=1479262#post1479262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question about Mage's magick, the spheres are pillars of reality, and according to Garou's lore the reality has been forged by the Triat. Does Triat using sphere to interact with universe, or are the sphere the creation of the Triat to &quot;maintain&quot; their work together?</div> </div> </div> </div>You made one wrong assumption and are still clinging to it: assuming Werewolf explains the universe.<br /> <br /> After understanding the other lines you can, indeed, assume it as true for your games and adapt things to conform, but for now that'll just make understanding Mage even more confusing for you.<br /> <br /> Forget the Triat. There is no Triat. Or Gaia. Each line is its own thing and own collection of assumptions about reality, and they're ultimately not compatible. While reading Mage, nothing from Werewolf is true or matters.<br /> <br /> Mages don't use <i>foci</i> to fool reality. They use <i>foci</i> to fool themselves. Reality can't be fooled, that's why Vulgar Magic gets you Paradox even without witnesses. Yet Paradox does not stop your Magic. The true nature of reality is mysterious and complicated, but let's just say it may be actually a gigantic spell woven and kept by the shared consciousness of humanity, including undergoing huge changes if this consciousness changes. Like how the Near Horizon shifted positions in the last decades materializing Mars, while as far as we can be sure the other planets may not actually exist yet in the material world, and a couple centuries ago the Moon didn't existed in the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T22:28:46-07:00","id":1479680,"title":"","content":"Well, WtA spirit entities like Celestines might exist in Mage for certain paradigms. But Mage is more complicated and these entities have different roles in Mage, then what the Garou believe to be true (and probably is true in a WtA game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T20:30:23-07:00","id":1479777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery?p=1479680#post1479680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, WtA spirit entities like Celestines might exist in Mage for certain paradigms. But Mage is more complicated and these entities have different roles in Mage, then what the Garou believe to be true (and probably is true in a WtA game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is perfectly possible to go full circle and end up with WtA's version of the world being true for your Mage game. But assuming it before actually understanding MtA just makes things too complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T14:08:55-07:00","id":1479833,"title":"","content":"It always seems akward to me, Vampire the mascarade, Werewolf the apocalypse, Mage the ascension all those book have a chapter about each other as antagonists. As player you can decide wich you decide to be the true version of the world but if you stay on the in-game explanation all those beings works with their own rules but they are incompatible with each others.<br /> <br /> As you said Mage rules work for them but if you try to combine them with Vampire or Werewolf, well you will have to work on a little conversion to make them fit together.<br /> I've heard about some crossovers of course but not for all version at the same times as far as i know.<br /> <br /> When we include them at our table we buy their book to know exactly what everyone is capable of, stay only on the antagonist chapter of each one isn't enough for us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 04-30-2022, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T14:25:23-07:00","id":1479835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479151-sorcery?p=1479833#post1479833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we include them at our table we buy their book to know exactly what everyone is capable of, stay only on the antagonist chapter of each one isn't enough for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, they're not just different creatures in the setting, they're different settings altogether, related, but not the same. That's why assuming the truths of one when reading the other is a pitfall, and will only get in the way of understanding them.<br /> <br /> And that's specially true for Mage, because Mage is really hard to wrap your mind around. It isn't necessarily best for that, or a better truth for the setting (as far as it can be said to have a truth), but it is really weird until you start to get a grip on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}